            <ArticleTitle>Glucose-enriched dialysate and tolerance to maintenance hemodialysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>10 patients entered a controlled 4-week study to evaluate the effect of a glucose-enriched dialysate (400 mg/100 ml) on hemodialysis tolerance. Headache during and after dialysis and post-dialysis fatigue decreased in a statistically significant manner. The average glycemia was only moderately increased with an adequate insulin response. Blood cholesterol and triglycerides did not vary signifcantly during this short study period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
